  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="503b054b-7d26-56d5-af59-bde486ddb097" activityNameId="2ee494a1-4b96-57ad-9768-18e3a39bc325" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Tablet, average, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Tablet, average, at plant
The data set represents the production of tablet with defined technical specifications; UUID: ef0274ee-89af-3f6f-8046-1c6a62ef198f
The dataset for average tablets, represented here as iPad Gen 2 with the weight of ~500 gr, is obtained from the LCA studies of Ahmadi Achachlouei et al., 2015; Teehan and Kandikar, 2013; and Hischier et al., 2015. The referred studies connect the lab-based data with the LCA database, i.e., Ecoinvent. This means that data is performed on the level of individual components (i.e., on the level of ICs, resistors, etc.) to build more precise inventory models for the device. The modeled tablet has a flash storage capacity of 256 GB and RAM capacity of 3 GB. According to the industry technology for IC tablets, up to 6 stacked dies can be integrated in a single package to optimize density and performance. In the modeling, the area of wafer/die is assumed to be ~10.2 cm2 to represent total wafer logic area according to the literature.
Location: Data for global average for tablets
Technology: The tablet has a processing unit, flash storage, RAM, and other connectivity features for standard tablets.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ef0274ee-89af-3f6f-8046-1c6a62ef198f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
